# WordPress development

Stack: WordPress, Roots Bedrock, Roots Sage, Blade, Tailwind CSS, ACF PRO, Vite, Lando. Theme: `web/app/themes/agency-starter`. Local site: `https://maison-form.lndo.site`. Admin: `/wp/wp-admin/`. Use `lando wp` from the project root. Do not print `.env`, `auth.json`, salts, or passwords.

## Architecture

Follow the installed Sage layout. Read an existing neighbor before adding a file.

- Shell: `resources/views/layouts/app.blade.php`. Header and footer: `resources/views/sections/header.blade.php` and `footer.blade.php`. Every public template uses that shell.
- Sections: `resources/views/components/sections/`. Shared chrome: `resources/views/components/`. Page assembly: `resources/views/partials/page-sections.blade.php`.
- Field registration: `app/fields/`. Rendering and escaping: `app/Acf/Content.php`. Variation class strings: `app/Design.php`.
- Keep markup in Blade components. Keep queries, field reads, escaping, and class lookup in PHP. Do not copy a section's markup into a second template.
- Use WordPress for posts, pages, the Journal posts page, `project` and `service` content, taxonomies, nav menus, and featured images. The content types live in `web/app/mu-plugins/heartwell-content.php`.

## Content

Client-facing headings, body copy, buttons, links, image references, and contact details come from WordPress core fields or ACF. Do not hardcode them in Blade or PHP.

- Modular page sections use the `page_sections` flexible content field.
- Repeatable rows use ACF repeaters. Galleries use ACF gallery fields.
- Sitewide header, footer, contact, and design choices live in one settings surface: `app/fields/site-settings.php`. That is the private Site Settings page today. When ACF PRO options pages are available, register one options page and move those fields there. Do not create a second settings store.
- ACF PRO is the required editor for flexible content, repeaters, galleries, and options pages. Do not download PRO, invent a license key, or put a key in the repo. If `acf_is_pro()` is false, keep the field definitions and stored meta, and say that the licensed editor is required. Do not replace missing PRO controls with hardcoded content.

## Styling

Tailwind CSS is the only CSS framework. Do not add Bootstrap, Bulma, or another utility or component framework.

- Tokens live in `resources/css/theme.css`. Reuse them. Add a token there before inventing a one-off color, size, or font.
- Write mobile-first utilities (`py-6 md:py-10`). Keep type on the existing heading and body scale.
- ACF variation choices must resolve through `App\Design::classes($group, $choice)`, which returns an allowlisted class string. Add the whole string to `Design::maps()`. Never concatenate a field value into a class name.

```php
// Correct
Design::classes('button', $choice);

// Wrong: builds an unreviewed class from stored content
'bg-' . $choice . '-500';
```

- Prefer Tailwind utilities. Add custom CSS only when utilities cannot express it, in `resources/css/theme.css`.
- One Vite config: `web/app/themes/agency-starter/vite.config.js`. One Tailwind entry: `resources/css/app.css`. Do not add a second Tailwind or Vite config. `app.css` and `editor.css` share one compiled stylesheet.

## Templates

Keep these pages on the shared header, navigation, footer, and tokens: Home (`front-page.blade.php`), Work, Studio, Services, Journal (`home.blade.php`, the posts page), and Contact. Keep `single-project.blade.php` and `single.blade.php` for one project and one journal article. Search and `404.blade.php` use the same shell.

## Implementation

Match WordPress and PHP coding standards. Escape on output (`esc_html`, `esc_attr`, `esc_url`, `wp_kses` for limited HTML). Sanitize and validate input. Use nonces and capability checks for state changes.

Keep one `h1`, a logical heading order, visible focus, labels on controls, meaningful image alt text, and a keyboard-operable mobile dialog. Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.

Serve attachment images with registered sizes and `srcset`. Lazy-load below-the-fold images. The LCP hero or featured image is `loading="eager"` with `fetchpriority="high"`. Do not enqueue the same CSS or JavaScript twice.

Preserve working behavior. Edit only files the task requires. Add a dependency only when the stack cannot do the job. Record a structural change in `README.md` or the matching doc in `docs/`.

For a new feature:

1. Read the existing component, field group, and template.
2. List the copy, media, and links an editor must change.
3. Reuse or add ACF fields. Flexible content for sections, repeaters for repeated rows.
4. Render them in Sage Blade, reusing a component.
5. Style with Tailwind and `Design::classes()`.
6. Check 375, 768, 1024, 1440, and 1920. No unintended horizontal scroll.
7. Edit the field in wp-admin and confirm the front end updates.
8. Run `npm run build --prefix web/app/themes/agency-starter` after CSS or JS changes. Confirm `public/build/manifest.json`. Leave `public/hot` only while the Vite dev server is running.
9. State what changed and where to edit it in WordPress.
